    "abstract": "Parts breakdown of the frame feet and their attachment to the cargo floor beams at stations C24 to C31, including the shear ties, the collars and the rivet standards used at each row.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "Illustrated parts breakdown of the frame foot fittings, shear ties and attachment hardware at stations C24 to C31 in the forward cargo compartment.",
      "figure_note": "The figure is drawn looking outboard at the left hand side; the right hand installation is the mirror image and uses the same part numbers. Item 10 is the foot fitting and it is common to all eight stations. The intercostal at item 30 is present only at the four stations where the floor beam pitch leaves the longest unsupported span, and the station list is on sheet 2. The rivet standard at item 50 differs between the inboard and outboard fastener rows and the figure identifies which row takes which."
    },
